Reproducible test you can run today:

CREATE TABLE t (id serial, grp int, val text);
INSERT INTO t (grp, val) SELECT g, md5(random()::text) FROM generate_series(1, 100000) g, generate_series(1, 10);
ANALYZE t;

EXPLAIN ANALYZE SELECT * FROM t WHERE grp = 50000;

Check the Seq Scan node. Estimated rows versus actual rows. What plan node surprised you? Reply with the numbers.

The fix is one command run during low traffic:

ANALYZE VERBOSE table_name;

This refreshes the statistics the planner uses. After this, the same query estimated 12,000 rows and chose a Hash Join with an Index Scan. Runtime dropped from 8 seconds to 47 milliseconds.
